WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Sara looked at Ermengarde, waiting to hear her friend's idea.

2
00:00:05.221 --> 00:00:11.469
"This afternoon I received a package from my favorite aunt," Ermengarde began.

3
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:16.128
She told Sara that the box was packed with wonderful treats.

4
00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:22.627
Cake, meat pies, and tarts. Buns, oranges, and chocolate.

5
00:00:22.628 --> 00:00:25.764
There was even apple cider to drink.

6
00:00:25.765 --> 00:00:28.553
Ermengarde was very excited.

7
00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:32.639
"I could sneak downstairs for the box, and bring it back here!"

8
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.524
Sara clutched Ermengarde's arm.

9
00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:40.609
"Do you really think you could? We could pretend to have a party.

10
00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:45.595
And, oh, won't you invite the prisoner in the next cell?"

11
00:00:45.596 --> 00:00:50.693
"Yes!" cried Ermengarde. "Let's knock on the wall now."

12
00:00:50.694 --> 00:00:54.352
Sara went to the wall and knocked five times.

13
00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:58.545
"That means come to my cell," she explained.

14
00:00:58.546 --> 00:01:01.628
The next moment Becky came through Sara's door.

15
00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:05.367
She stopped short when she saw Ermengarde.

16
00:01:05.368 --> 00:01:10.780
"It's all right," said Sara. "Miss Ermengarde wants you to be here.

17
00:01:10.781 --> 00:01:14.310
She's going to bring us a box of food."

18
00:01:14.311 --> 00:01:18.114
"To eat?" Becky's eyes widened.

19
00:01:18.115 --> 00:01:21.780
"Yes, and we're going to have a party!"

20
00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:26.668
Ermengarde hurried away so quickly that she dropped her red shawl.

21
00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:34.262
"Sometimes just before things get to their worst, something wonderful happens," Sara said.

22
00:01:34.263 --> 00:01:39.444
"It's like magic. Now let's set the table for the party."

23
00:01:39.445 --> 00:01:43.960
"But what will we use?" asked Becky.

24
00:01:43.961 --> 00:01:48.420
"Ermengarde's shawl can be the tablecloth," Sara said.

25
00:01:48.421 --> 00:01:51.941
"I'll look in the old trunk I had when I was a princess.

26
00:01:51.942 --> 00:01:55.950
I'm sure I'll find more things that we can use!"

27
00:01:55.951 --> 00:02:00.703
Becky covered the table with the shawl while Sara opened her old trunk.

28
00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:03.970
Inside she found some white handkerchiefs.

29
00:02:03.971 --> 00:02:06.225
Sara ran to the table.

30
00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:13.677
"Let's pretend these are plates made of finest china!"

31
00:02:13.678 --> 00:02:18.177
The girls decorated the table with flowers from a straw hat.

32
00:02:18.178 --> 00:02:23.271
They used some scraps of paper to make a tiny fire in the fireplace.

33
00:02:23.272 --> 00:02:28.539
Sara turned suddenly to see Becky standing by the table with her eyes shut.

34
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.885
There was an odd look on Becky's face.

35
00:02:31.886 --> 00:02:35.600
"What's the matter, Becky?" Sara asked.

36
00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:41.474
Becky opened her eyes. "I was pretending it was a real banquet, miss.

37
00:02:41.475 --> 00:02:45.193
Just like you do. It almost worked."

38
00:02:45.194 --> 00:02:50.929
Sara laughed. "Keep practicing, Becky!"

39
00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:55.411
When Ermengarde returned, she gazed around with delight.

40
00:02:55.412 --> 00:03:02.021
"Oh, Sara! You're so clever! It looks like a real party up here!"

41
00:03:02.022 --> 00:03:07.866
"It's like a queen's table," said Becky with a happy sigh.

42
00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:12.591
"We're pretending to hold a banquet in a castle."

43
00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:17.735
"Ermengarde, you must be the princess!" Sara insisted.

44
00:03:17.736 --> 00:03:22.000
"No, that's your role," Ermengarde said.

45
00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:28.847
Sara grinned. "Well then, let's begin the feast!"

46
00:03:28.848 --> 00:03:34.351
The girls sat down. They had just begun to eat when they heard a noise.

47
00:03:34.352 --> 00:03:39.596
All three sprang to their feet. Someone was coming up the stairs!

48
00:03:39.597 --> 00:03:43.360
And they all recognized the angry footsteps at once.

49
00:03:43.361 --> 00:03:48.935
When Miss Minchin threw open the door, her face was pale with rage.

50
00:03:48.936 --> 00:03:54.230
"So Lavinia was telling the truth!" declared the headmistress.

51
00:03:54.231 --> 00:03:57.411
"Something is going on up here!"

52
00:03:57.412 --> 00:04:00.680
Sara and Ermengarde looked at each other.

53
00:04:00.681 --> 00:04:05.379
Lavinia had guessed their secret and told Miss Minchin.

54
00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:11.650
The headmistress slapped Becky. "You're fired! You'll leave tomorrow!"

55
00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:14.350
Becky ran from the room.

56
00:04:14.351 --> 00:04:18.938
Sara stood quite still, but Ermengarde burst into tears.

57
00:04:18.939 --> 00:04:22.849
"Don't send Becky away," cried Ermengarde.

58
00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:27.617
"My aunt mailed me the package. We're only having a party."

59
00:04:27.618 --> 00:04:31.411
"So I see!" Miss Minchin snapped.

60
00:04:31.412 --> 00:04:37.431
"With the Princess Sara at the head of the table!" She glared at Sara.

61
00:04:37.432 --> 00:04:43.355
"You're the one behind this. Ermengarde wouldn't think of such a thing.

62
00:04:43.356 --> 00:04:49.820
I'll deal with you tomorrow. You won't have anything to eat all day."

63
00:04:49.821 --> 00:04:55.117
"I haven't had much to eat today," Sara said quietly.

64
00:04:55.118 --> 00:04:59.366
Miss Minchin ignored her and scolded Ermengarde.

65
00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:04.213
"You've brought your beautiful new books into this dirty attic.

66
00:05:04.214 --> 00:05:06.853
Take them back to your room.

67
00:05:06.854 --> 00:05:11.831
You'll stay there all day tomorrow, and I'm going to write to your father.

68
00:05:11.832 --> 00:05:15.628
What would he say if he knew where you are tonight?"

69
00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:20.646
Something in Sara's gaze got Miss Minchin's attention.

70
00:05:20.647 --> 00:05:23.732
Miss Minchin spun back toward Sara.

71
00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:26.925
"What are you thinking about?" she demanded.

72
00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.772
"Why are you looking at me like that?"

73
00:05:29.773 --> 00:05:33.019
Sara responded in a low voice.

74
00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:38.199
"What would my father say if he knew where I am tonight?"

75
00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.374
"How dare you!" Miss Minchin flew at Sara and shook her.

76
00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:46.257
"Go to bed right now!"

77
00:05:46.258 --> 00:05:48.863
The headmistress picked up the books.

78
00:05:48.864 --> 00:05:53.562
Then she swept the food into the box and shoved it at Ermengarde.

79
00:05:53.563 --> 00:05:57.070
Pushing Ermengarde ahead of her, she left the room.

80
00:05:57.071 --> 00:06:00.806
Sara was left standing alone in her room.

81
00:06:00.807 --> 00:06:06.092
The last spark had died out in the fire.

82
00:06:06.093 --> 00:06:12.306
The table now looked like nothing more than some old handkerchiefs and fake flowers.

83
00:06:12.307 --> 00:06:14.852
Sara turned to her doll.

84
00:06:14.853 --> 00:06:20.369
"There isn't any party left," she said sadly to Emily.

85
00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:24.062
Then she climbed into bed and closed her eyes.

86
00:06:24.063 --> 00:06:31.197
She didn't see the face peering at her through the skylight.

